.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt ITHWM 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ithwm
.Nd hardware monitor driver for the ITE IT8613E Super I/O chip
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "device superio"
.Cd "device ithwm"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver exposes temperature sensors, fan speed counters, and voltage inputs
from the hardware monitor logical device (LDN 4) of the ITE IT8613E
Super I/O chip
via
.Xr sysctl 8 .
.Pp
To load the driver as a module at boot time, add the following line to
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ithwm_load="YES"
.Ed
.Pp
Register access uses the 8-byte I/O window provided by the
.Xr superio 4
bus via an index/data port pair.
.Sh HARDWARE
The
.Nm
driver supports the following Super I/O hardware monitor chips:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
ITE IT8613E
.El
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
The following read-only
.Xr sysctl 8
variables are provided under
.Va dev.ithwm.<unit> :
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va temp0 , temp1 , temp2
Temperature sensor readings, reported using the
.Dq IK
(decikelvin) sysctl format as used by
.Xr amdtemp 4
and
.Xr lm75 4 .
Sensors that read as not connected at attach time are not exposed.
.It Va fan0 Ns .. Ns Va fan4
Fan tachometer readings in RPM.
A value of 0 indicates a stalled or absent fan.
.It Va vin0 Ns .. Ns Va vin7
Voltage input readings in millivolts.
Each ADC LSB represents 11 mV.
On-board voltage dividers for higher-voltage rails are board-specific
and internal scaling of some inputs is not applied;
raw scaled millivolt values are reported.
.It Va vbat
Battery voltage in millivolts.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr amdtemp 4 ,
.Xr itwd 4 ,
.Xr lm75 4 ,
.Xr superio 4 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
